Study on Taekwondo Athletes’ Resting State and Movement of Left Whirlwind Kicks’ Stability, Posture and Synchronicity Oscillation Spectrum

Wu Lei

(Wusong Jiang School Kunshan Jiangsu 215300, China) Abstract: Objective: To compare taekwondo athletes' resting state and complete left whirlwind kick after the general stability, as well as the postural sway spectrum and synchronization to analysis of left whirlwind kick on the balance ability of Taekwondo athletes. Methods: Eight elite taekwondo athletes were chosen from Shandong Sports college. It used the Tetrax balance test system test subjects resting state and completed three consecutive times after left whirlwind kick, which is 4 different stability index condition (ST) and postural sway spectrum synchronization, including open the natural stand (NO), eyes closed, natural stand (NC), open foot stand (PO), eyes closed foot stand (PC). Results: Complete left whirlwind kick athletes' ST was significantly higher than that in resting state ST values of 3 consecutive times (P=0.043). Through analysis of postural sway spectrum, taekwondo athletes postural sway from F1 to F8 showed a decreasing trend after complete left whirlwind kick;
